{"nodes": [{"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_captures_inputs_gemini_inputs_gemini", "label": "M's Gemini inputs, held in full (register 1616)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/captures/INPUTS-GEMINI.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Status SECONDARY ACCOUNT: nothing here is a source. The content is held so a later session can re-read the original framing rather than the summary of it, and so nobody re-derives a judgement already made."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_captures_inputs_gemini_input1_temperature_axis", "label": "Input 1 \u2014 Temperature and the (n, l, k, T) index", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/captures/INPUTS-GEMINI.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Not automatically refused because T differs from the penetration regime in the way that matters: the regime is a function of (Z, charge, l) and T is not \u2014 a cell can be at any temperature. So the closure test has not been run and its answer is not predictable."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_captures_inputs_gemini_input2_catalytic_transition", "label": "Input 2 \u2014 spacetime transition as catalytic phase change", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/captures/INPUTS-GEMINI.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No object in any index here; kept for its transferable shape \u2014 a small precise perturbation releasing latent structure already present, which is S.seed's shape."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_captures_inputs_gemini_input3_zero_energy_trigger", "label": "Input 3 \u2014 the zero-energy projective trigger", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/captures/INPUTS-GEMINI.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The pointers (Aharonov-Bohm, Bell-state measurement, Chern number toggling, Landauer) are real physics; the claim has no object here. What transfers is the distinction between an operation that moves a system and one that re-indexes it \u2014 coordinate versus key."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_captures_inputs_gemini_input4_dual_aspect_monism", "label": "Input 4 \u2014 dual-aspect monism and the 14D hierarchy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/captures/INPUTS-GEMINI.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "What is shared is the SHAPE \u2014 a system whose state determines what it can reach, whose boundary is maintained by refusing operations, and whose growth is monotone. That autopoiesis and A.cert both arrive there is real and is not evidence either explains the other."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_captures_inputs_gemini_input5_three_body_lowdin", "label": "Input 5 \u2014 the three-body problem and the L\u00f6wdin challenge", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/captures/INPUTS-GEMINI.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The figure-8 choreography benchmark is well-posed and CHAPTER-THREEBODY.md does not attempt it. The offered L\u00f6wdin test (derive the 4s/3d crossover from geometry) is worth keeping distinct from deriving n+l, because the chapter's finding is that n+l is the wrong target and the order is the right one."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_captures_inputs_gemini_input6_montgomery_odlyzko", "label": "Input 6 \u2014 Montgomery-Odlyzko and GUE statistics", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/captures/INPUTS-GEMINI.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The hit that matters is not the zeta function but Rosenzweig-Porter 1960, which states the keyability problem of register 1597 in 1960. The application to our own data failed its control."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_captures_inputs_gemini_a_cert", "label": "A.cert \u2014 the four admitted operations", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/captures/INPUTS-GEMINI.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Admits only relabel, re-coordinatise, refine a fibration, drop a coordinate. It is a boundary maintained by refusing operations, which is why adding a fifth is the question every proposal has to answer."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_captures_inputs_gemini_capacity_identity", "label": "The capacity identity \u03a32n\u00b2 = N(N+1)(2N+1)/3", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/captures/INPUTS-GEMINI.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_captures_inputs_gemini_bott_inversion", "label": "The 14D closure argument is backwards", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/captures/INPUTS-GEMINI.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bott periodicity is real, but periodicity says the structure REPEATS \u2014 which gives no residue privileged status and is precisely a reason a hierarchy does not terminate."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_captures_inputs_gemini_markov_blanket_test", "label": "The Markov blanket test and its caveat", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/captures/INPUTS-GEMINI.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "210 witnessed cells touch the exterior directly, so the closure does not separate \u2014 but the test was ADJACENCY and a blanket is defined by conditional independence, with no measure on these cells to condition on."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_captures_inputs_gemini_rosenzweig_porter_1960", "label": "Rosenzweig & Porter, Repulsion of Energy Levels in Complex Atomic Spectra (1960)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/captures/INPUTS-GEMINI.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_captures_inputs_gemini_lowdin_1969", "label": "L\u00f6wdin 1969 \u2014 the n+l derivation as an unsolved problem", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/captures/INPUTS-GEMINI.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_captures_inputs_gemini_allen_knight_2002", "label": "Allen & Knight, Int. J. Quantum Chem. 90, 80 (2002)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/captures/INPUTS-GEMINI.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_captures_inputs_gemini_scerri_2009", "label": "Scerri, Int. J. Quantum Chem. 109, 959 (2009) \u2014 ~20 exceptions", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/captures/INPUTS-GEMINI.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_captures_inputs_gemini_figure8_choreography", "label": "The figure-8 choreography benchmark (Chenciner & Montgomery)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/captures/INPUTS-GEMINI.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_captures_inputs_gemini_gue_control_failure", "label": "The GUE/GOE r-statistic control failure", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/captures/INPUTS-GEMINI.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A pure 1/n\u00b2 Rydberg series with no chaos in it scores 0.644 against the grouped 0.539, so the statistic measures the series law and not level repulsion. The control, not the match, is what settled it."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_captures_inputs_gemini_null_matrix_unheld", "label": "The 36-cell null matrix \u2014 an object not held here", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/captures/INPUTS-GEMINI.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No such object exists in mathreg or any index here. If M has a source for it, it needs one; otherwise it is not ours."}], "edges": [{"source": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_captures_inputs_gemini_inputs_gemini", "target": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_captures_inputs_gemini_input1_temperature_axis", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/captures/INPUTS-GEMINI.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_captures_inputs_gemini_inputs_gemini", "target": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_captures_inputs_gemini_input2_catalytic_transition", "rel